---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Stillware Ltd"
  description="How Stillware Ltd handles your data. Local-first architecture means your data stays on your device."
>
    <article class="legal-page">
        <header class="legal-hero">
            <div class="container"><h1>Privacy Policy</h1></div>
        </header>
        <div class="legal-body">
            <div class="container">
                <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> October 31, 2026</p>
                <p><strong>Company:</strong> Stillware Ltd</p>
                <p>Stillware Ltd ("we", "our", or "us") builds software you own. We believe that your private data—whether it is financial ledgers, personal journals, home inventories, or health records—belongs exclusively to you.</p>
                <p>This Privacy Policy explains our strict, privacy-first approach to information across all Stillware Ltd applications (including Zeroed and all future releases).</p>

                <div class="highlight">
                    <p><strong>Core Principle: Local-First &amp; Zero Telemetry</strong></p>
                    <p>All Stillware applications are built on a "local-first" architecture. The data you create inside our apps is stored directly on your physical device. We do not have servers that host, process, or read your personal app data, and we utilize zero telemetry or behavioral tracking. The one exception is RankUp Chess's optional grown-up sign-in, described in section 4.</p>
                </div>

                <h2>1. Information Collection and Use</h2>
                <h3>Your Application Data</h3>
                <p>Whatever data you input into a Stillware app (e.g., transactions, text entries, photos, audio logs) is encrypted and saved strictly to your local device storage. We do not collect, transmit, or have access to this data.</p>

                <h3>Data Synchronization (Your Cloud, Your Rules)</h3>
                <p>Many Stillware apps offer cross-device synchronization using your personal cloud storage (such as Google Drive or Apple iCloud).</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>How it works:</strong> Our apps communicate directly with your personal cloud provider to sync an encrypted backup of your local database.</li>
                    <li><strong>Our Access:</strong> We request the strictest, most limited permissions available (e.g., the <code>drive.file</code> scope on Google Drive). This means our apps can only access the specific sync folders they create. We cannot view, edit, or delete any other files in your personal cloud.</li>
                    <li><strong>Your Control:</strong> You retain ultimate ownership. You can revoke the app's access or delete the sync folders from your personal cloud at any time.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>On-Device Processing</h3>
                <p>Some of our apps utilize Machine Learning (like receipt scanning, OCR text extraction, or image filtering). All processing happens locally on your device's hardware. No images, text, or audio are ever sent to our servers for processing.</p>

                <h3>Purchases, Licence Activation and Free Trials</h3>
                <p>Direct downloads (Windows and Mac) are sold through Paddle, which acts as Merchant of Record: Paddle collects your payment and billing details and is responsible for them under its own privacy policy. When a purchase completes, Paddle tells our licence service the transaction reference. The service creates a licence key and emails it to the address you gave Paddle, using Resend to deliver the message. We use your email address only for that one message and do not store it in our licence records. If the message cannot be sent at once, we keep it, encrypted, and try again every hour: it is deleted as soon as it is sent, and within 25 hours at the latest.</p>
                <p>Our licence records hold a one-way hash of your licence key, the Paddle transaction reference, the product, and for each device you activate the identifier the app reads from that computer (the operating system's own machine ID, such as the Windows MachineGuid or the Mac's hardware UUID) and the activation dates. They do not hold your name, your email address, the name of your device, or anything you enter into an app. The exception is the scrambled address a grown-up links for RankUp Chess (section 4). To stop a free trial restarting when an app is reinstalled, the trial service also records a device identifier and the date the trial began. These records let us limit a licence to a set number of devices, let you move it to a new one, and keep trials fair.</p>

                <h3>Website &amp; Blog Analytics</h3>
                <p>The stillwareltd.com website uses <a href="https://umami.is" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Umami</a> Cloud, a cookieless analytics service, to count visits and to measure which pages lead to an app-store listing or download. It sets no cookies in your browser. It receives the page you viewed, the page that referred you, your browser, operating system, screen size and language, an approximate location such as your country, and events such as clicking an app-store link or playing an embedded video. Umami states that it does not collect personally identifiable information and that visitors cannot be identified or tracked across websites. We use the data only for aggregate reporting. If your browser sends a Do Not Track signal, the tracker sends nothing, and you can also block it with your browser's tracking protection or an extension. None of this applies to our apps, which contain no analytics or telemetry (see above). We do not use Meta Pixels, Google Analytics or advertising trackers on the website.</p>

                <h3>Support Communications</h3>
                <p>When you contact us for technical support, we receive your email address and any information you voluntarily provide in your message. We use this information exclusively to assist you and resolve your issue.</p>

                <h2>2. Website Communications &amp; Newsletters ("Join the Rebellion")</h2>
                <p>We offer voluntary email subscriptions on our website (stillwareltd.com) so you can be notified when we launch new apps, release major updates, or publish a new free printable: one email when we ship something, at most once a month. Nothing on this website asks for your email before you can download it. Every free printable, guide and kit downloads directly.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>What we collect:</strong> If you choose to subscribe to our newsletter, we collect the email address you provide, the date, and which page's form you used. Our newsletter service, Buttondown, also records the technical details it needs to prevent abuse, such as the IP address the form was sent from and the referring page. If you ask to be notified about an upcoming app (such as a waitlist), that form stores only your email address, with our host, Netlify (Netlify Forms).</li>
                    <li><strong>Confirming:</strong> We send one email asking you to confirm, and a reminder 24 hours later if you have not. Nothing else is sent until you confirm. After you confirm, we send one welcome email.</li>
                    <li><strong>How we use it:</strong> We use this email address strictly to send you the specific communications you requested. Open and click tracking are switched off: our emails contain no invisible tracking pixels, links are not rewritten to see who clicks, and we do not profile your reading habits. Links to our own website carry a campaign label (utm_source) so our website analytics can count visits from the newsletter in total, never by person. Our website analytics (Umami, above) also counts that a newsletter form was sent and from which page, without the address.</li>
                    <li><strong>Who handles it:</strong> Buttondown, LLC, in the United States, stores the list and sends the emails for us, under its <a href="https://buttondown.com/legal/data-processing-agreement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">data processing agreement</a> and <a href="https://buttondown.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.</li>
                    <li><strong>Our Promise:</strong> We will never sell, rent, or trade your email address to third-party marketers, data brokers, or advertisers.</li>
                    <li><strong>Your Control:</strong> We send the newsletter only with your consent, and you can withdraw it at any time: click the "Unsubscribe" link at the bottom of any email we send you, reply to any email, or contact support. Upon unsubscribing, your email is removed from our active mailing list at once. Buttondown keeps a record that the address unsubscribed so it is never emailed again by mistake; ask us and we will delete it entirely.</li>
                    <li><strong>Separation of Data:</strong> Your newsletter subscription is managed entirely separately from our applications. Subscribing to our website does not link your email address to your encrypted, local app data. The newsletter is for adults: RankUp Chess, our app for children, never asks for it.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>3. Third-Party Services</h2>
                <p>Because we do not host your data, our use of third-party services is strictly limited to facilitating purchases and app functionality:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Payment Processors (Paddle, Apple App Store, Google Play):</strong> These services process your payments and act as the Merchant of Record. We do not collect or store your credit card details.</li>
                    <li><strong>Resend:</strong> Our email delivery provider, which sends your licence key email, and RankUp Chess's sign-in codes and confirmations. It keeps delivery records of those messages under its own privacy policy.</li>
                    <li><strong>Netlify and Turso:</strong> Netlify hosts this website and the licence service, and Turso hosts the database that holds the licence and trial records described above.</li>
                    <li><strong>Buttondown:</strong> Our newsletter service, which stores the newsletter list and sends the newsletter (section 2).</li>
                    <li><strong>RevenueCat:</strong> We use RevenueCat to manage purchase histories and validate lifetime licenses across devices. They may collect anonymous App User IDs and anonymous purchase receipts, but this is never linked to your actual app data. For RankUp Chess, RevenueCat also tells our licence service about "Every device" purchases, by the anonymous ID, so a family can restore them on another device.</li>
                    <li><strong>Cloud APIs (Google Drive / Apple iCloud):</strong> Used solely to route your encrypted data between your own devices.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>YouTube API Services</h3>
                <p>Stillware Ltd publishes budgeting and chess videos on its own YouTube channels, <a href="https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCEvncfxFpbDNXkHbeucU75A">Zeroed: Offline Budget Planner</a> and <a href="https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC7r19r2thTxTgzxzFu3aNpQ">RankUp Chess</a>. To do this we operate an internal publishing tool that uses <strong>YouTube API Services</strong> to upload videos, thumbnails, subtitles and playlist entries to those channels, and to read public YouTube data (video titles, view counts and search results) when planning new videos. By using or interacting with our YouTube channel you are also bound by the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms">YouTube Terms of Service</a>, and Google's handling of your data is described in the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>No viewer data is collected.</strong> The tool authenticates only our own channel's Google account. It does not access, collect or store any data about YouTube users, viewers, subscribers or commenters, and it does not read private data from any account other than our own.</li>
                    <li><strong>What is stored:</strong> the channel's OAuth access token (on a single company computer, never on a server), the identifiers of the videos we uploaded, and aggregate public statistics about videos (view counts, like counts, durations) retained for no longer than 30 days for editorial planning. No personal information is stored.</li>
                    <li><strong>No sharing:</strong> nothing obtained through YouTube API Services is sold, shared with third parties, or used for advertising.</li>
                    <li><strong>Revoking access:</strong> the channel owner can revoke the tool's access at any time from the <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google security settings page</a>. Anyone who believes we hold data about them obtained through YouTube API Services may contact <a href="mailto:support@stillwareltd.com">support@stillwareltd.com</a> and it will be deleted within 30 days.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2 id="rankup-chess">4. RankUp Chess, Our App for Children</h2>
                <p>RankUp Chess is a chess app made for children. This section explains, for parents, what it does with information.</p>
                <div class="highlight">
                    <p><strong>The short version</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Nothing about your child is collected. Names, games, lessons and progress stay on the device.</li>
                        <li>RankUp Chess has no ads, no chat, no accounts, no analytics and no tracking.</li>
                        <li>Anything that spends money, opens a web page, shares a file or changes a grown-up setting asks a grown-up first.</li>
                        <li>A grown-up may give us their own email to restore a purchase on another device, only with a parent's agreement given by email. It is never needed to play, and it can be removed in the app at any time.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>What Stays on the Device</h3>
                <p>A child's profile is a name that the child or a grown-up chooses, an avatar and an age group. Their games, lessons, puzzles, stars, ratings and settings, the grown-up PIN and any limits a grown-up sets are kept in the app on that device. We never receive them.</p>

                <h3>What Leaves the Device Only When a Grown-Up Sends It</h3>
                <p>Backups, data exports, certificates, the weekly report and friend codes are made on the device. They leave it only when a grown-up shares them, after the grown-up check, with the app the grown-up chooses. We do not receive them.</p>

                <h3>Who Receives What</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>The app stores (Google Play, and the App Store on iPhone and iPad):</strong> Google or Apple take the payment. We never see your card or your name.</li>
                    <li><strong>RevenueCat</strong>, which handles in-app purchases for us. It receives an anonymous ID that its library creates on the device (not linked to a name or an email address), the purchase receipt, and the device's language and currency. It uses them to tell the app that the purchase was made. RevenueCat states that it collects no diagnostics, no location and nothing a child does in the app. What it keeps is described in <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RevenueCat's privacy policy</a>.</li>
                    <li><strong>Windows and Mac downloads</strong> are sold through Paddle. When a key is activated on a computer, the app sends the key and the computer's machine ID, as described in "Purchases, Licence Activation and Free Trials" in section 1. Versions before 0.11.0 also send the computer's name, which our licence service ignores and does not store; from 0.11.0 the app no longer sends it.</li>
                    <li><strong>Our licence service</strong> (Stillware Ltd, hosted by Netlify, with its database at Turso). It records that an "Every device" purchase was made, by the anonymous ID above, the product, the store and the date. We use that ID and these records only to process and restore purchases: never to contact anyone, to build a profile or to show ads. If a grown-up signs in or adds their email, the service also handles that email as described below.</li>
                    <li><strong>Resend</strong>, which sends the sign-in codes and the confirmation emails for us.</li>
                    <li><strong>Paddle</strong>, for a purchase made on our website. We ask Paddle whether a typed email matches a purchase. Paddle already holds the buyer's email; we copy nothing.</li>
                    <li>We do not use any analytics, crash-reporting or advertising service in the app.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Children</h3>
                <p>Stillware does not knowingly collect personal information from children. RankUp Chess is made for children, so we built it so that a child never has to give us anything: there is no account or sign-in for a child, no chat, no ads and no online play. Purchases, links out of the app, sharing and backups are behind a grown-up check. The only personal information we ask for is a grown-up's own email: only if a grown-up chooses to give it, and only with a parent's agreement, given by email (below).</p>

                <h3>The Grown-Up's Email (Optional)</h3>
                <p><strong>Why we ask.</strong> Only to let a family restore a purchase they already made, on another device. We use the email for nothing else.</p>
                <p><strong>When we ask.</strong> Only if a grown-up chooses, behind the grown-up check. It is under Restore Purchases ("Already own RankUp on another device?"). After a grown-up buys "Every device" in a store, the app also offers "Add your email so your other devices can restore". It is never needed to play.</p>
                <p><strong>How a parent agrees.</strong> RankUp Chess is made for children, so we treat an email typed into it as if a child might have typed it, and we ask the address's owner first.</p>
                <ol>
                    <li>We send a 6-digit code to the address. The email says why the address was typed, what we keep, who handles it and how to agree, and links this policy. For a sign-in, the code goes only if a purchase matches the address.</li>
                    <li>Entering the code in the app and tapping "Agree and sign in" (or "Agree and add email") is the agreement. If the code is not entered, nothing is kept: the request is deleted within 25 hours.</li>
                    <li>We then send a confirmation email that says what happened and how to take the agreement back.</li>
                </ol>
                <p><strong>What we keep.</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>For a sign-in:</strong> no copy of the address. We send the device a signed note that says this household owns RankUp Chess. The note holds no email, no name and no device ID.</li>
                    <li><strong>For an added email:</strong> a scrambled form of the address, made with a secret key so that it cannot be turned back into the address, next to the anonymous purchase number. We also note which version of this notice was agreed to, and when. We keep no readable copy.</li>
                    <li><strong>For a purchase on our website:</strong> Paddle holds the email. We ask Paddle whether it matches a purchase and keep nothing.</li>
                    <li><strong>On the device:</strong> nothing but the signed note.</li>
                    <li><strong>Codes:</strong> a salted hash with its expiry, never the code itself.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>We say the same thing to everyone who asks, whether or not their email matches a purchase, so nobody can use the app to find out whose email we hold.</p>
                <p><strong>What we do not do.</strong> We do not use the email for marketing. We do not sell it, rent it or share it with anyone but the services named in "Who Receives What", each bound by written terms to use it only for us. We do not send it to RevenueCat or to the app stores. We do not join it to anything about a child, because we hold nothing about a child.</p>

                <h3>How Long We Keep It</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>A code request</strong>, also for an address that matched nothing: kept to check the code, and deleted within 25 hours of the code no longer working (a code works for 10 minutes, once).</li>
                    <li><strong>A count of requests</strong> from an address or a network address, scrambled: kept to stop abuse, and deleted within 25 hours.</li>
                    <li><strong>A confirmation email that could not be sent at once</strong>: kept, encrypted, so it can be tried again every hour, and deleted as soon as it is sent, and within 25 hours at the latest. A code email is never kept: you ask for a new code instead.</li>
                    <li><strong>An added email</strong>, scrambled, and its link to the purchase: kept so the family can sign in on another device. Deleted 24 months after its last sign-in, at once when you remove it, and at once if the purchase is refunded.</li>
                    <li><strong>A store purchase's anonymous record:</strong> it is the purchase, so it is kept while RankUp Chess is sold and for up to 12 months after. A refunded purchase is deleted 13 months after the refund. We delete any of them on request.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3 id="rankup-chess-delete">Taking It Back, and Your Rights</h3>
                <p>You can take back your agreement at any time:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>in RankUp Chess: Settings → Restore Purchases → Remove my email. It is behind the grown-up check, and we send a code to the address to make sure it is yours;</li>
                    <li>or reply to any of our emails, or write to <a href="mailto:support@stillwareltd.com">support@stillwareltd.com</a>.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Removing the email deletes every form of it we hold. It does not remove your purchase, and devices that already have Premium keep it. You may also ask what we hold, ask us to correct or delete it, and tell us to collect nothing more. We answer within 30 days. You may complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Information Commissioner's Office</a> or, in the US, to the <a href="https://www.ftc.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Federal Trade Commission</a>.</p>

                <h2>5. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
                <p>Because Stillware Ltd does not host user accounts or store your app data on our servers, we cannot "delete your account" in the traditional cloud-software sense: there is no account and no app data to delete. The only records we hold are the small licence and trial records described in section 1 (no name or email), and for RankUp Chess the scrambled address a grown-up links and the anonymous purchase records (section 4, with how long each is kept). Remove the address in the app, or email us. If you want a licence record removed, email <a href="mailto:support@stillwareltd.com">support@stillwareltd.com</a> with your Paddle receipt reference. Removing it ends that licence, so we will confirm with you first. Purchase records held by Paddle, Apple and Google are governed by their own policies.</p>
                <p><strong>To completely and permanently destroy your data:</strong></p>
                <ol>
                    <li>Delete the specific Stillware application(s) from your device(s).</li>
                    <li>Log in to your personal cloud provider (Google Drive, iCloud) and delete the app-specific data folder (e.g., <code>ZeroedData</code>).</li>
                </ol>

                <h2>6. Security</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Local Encryption:</strong> Where applicable, your databases are encrypted on-device using industry-standard protocols (such as AES-256) before they are ever synced to your personal cloud.</li>
                    <li><strong>Transit Security:</strong> All communication between your device and your cloud provider, or your device and our payment processors, occurs over secure HTTPS (SSL/TLS) connections.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
                <p>While Stillware Ltd designs some offline-native applications specifically intended to be safe, secure sandboxes for children and teenagers, we do not collect personal information from children. Our apps keep what a child creates on the device and do not send it to our servers, so we have no way to collect, store or share it. The one exception is RankUp Chess's optional grown-up sign-in, which asks a grown-up, behind a grown-up check, for their own email, with a parent's agreement given by email. Nothing about a child is sent. RankUp Chess, our app for children, is described in section 4.</p>

                <h2>8. Beta Testing &amp; Feedback</h2>
                <p>If you participate in a Stillware Beta Exchange, we may collect your email address, device OS, and written feedback to improve the product and grant you a lifetime software license.</p>
                <div class="highlight">
                    <p>Your email and feedback are <strong>never</strong> linked to your in-app data.</p>
                </div>
                <p>You may request the deletion of your beta feedback or email from our contact records at any time by emailing support.</p>

                <h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
                <p>As we release new applications, we may update this Privacy Policy. We will notify users of any material changes by posting the new version on this page and updating the "Effective Date." Because we do not require user accounts, checking this page is the best way to stay informed.</p>

                <h2>10. Contact Us</h2>
                <p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or how your data is handled, please contact us at:</p>
                <p><a href="mailto:support@stillwareltd.com">support@stillwareltd.com</a></p>
                <p>Stillware Ltd, registered in England and Wales (company number 16927952). Registered office: 155 Dugdale Hill Lane, Potters Bar, England, EN6 2DF. Phone: <a href="tel:+447438371722">+44 7438 371722</a>.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </article>
</Layout>

<style>
    .legal-hero {
        padding: 12rem 0 3rem;
        background: var(--gradient-obsidian);
        text-align: center;
    }

    .legal-hero h1 { color: #ffffff; font-size: 3rem; }

    .legal-body {
        padding: 3rem 0 6rem;
        max-width: 800px;
        margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .legal-body h2 { margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .legal-body h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: 1.2rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; color: #34495e; }
    .legal-body p { margin-bottom: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; }
    .legal-body ul, .legal-body ol { margin: 1rem 0; padding-left: 1.5rem; }
    .legal-body li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; line-height: 1.6; }
    .legal-body code { background: var(--color-surface); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; }
    .legal-body a { color: var(--color-primary); text-decoration: underline; }

    .highlight {
        background: rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.04);
        padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
        border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary);
        border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
        margin: 1.5rem 0;
    }

    .highlight p { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    .highlight p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
</style>
